      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1261",
      "html": "<p>Malapterurus oguensis Sauvage, 1879. Type locality: Ogôoué River at Duomé, Congo [should be Gabon]. Size: 215 mm SL. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2009).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1261",
      "html": "<p>Africa: known from the Ogôoué basin, Nyanga River and Kouilou-Niari system (Cameroon to Gabon).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1261",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1261",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: Malapterurus comes from the Greek malakos, meaning soft, pteron, meaning fin and oura, meaning tail; presumably in reference to the adipose fin, which appears all the more prominent in the absence of the rayed dorsal fin.</p>"
    },
    {
